1
00:00:00,680 --> 00:00:02,750
(Sheldon:)I'm nauseated
and feverish.

2
00:00:02,750 --> 00:00:05,670
(Sheldon:)I believe I may have cholera.

3
00:00:05,670 --> 00:00:07,970
(Leonard:)There's no cholera
in Pasadena.

4
00:00:07,970 --> 00:00:09,020
(Leonard:)Just like last summer,

5
00:00:09,020 --> 00:00:11,090
(Leonard:)when there
was no malaria
in Pasadena.

6
00:00:11,090 --> 00:00:12,480
(Sheldon:)Well, if it's not cholera,

7
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:15,380
(Sheldon:)then based on a quick
Internet search,

8
00:00:15,380 --> 00:00:18,220
(Sheldon:)the other explanations in
decreasing order of likelihood

9
00:00:18,220 --> 00:00:22,100
(Sheldon:)are Hirschsprung's Disease,
botulism, a 30-foot tapeworm

10
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:26,020
(Sheldon:)or accidental ingestion
of chrysanthemum blossoms.

11
00:00:26,020 --> 00:00:29,830
(Leonard:)When would you have accidentally
eaten chrysanthemum blossoms?

12
00:00:29,830 --> 00:00:31,410
(Sheldon:)It's part of an
unlikely scenario

13
00:00:31,410 --> 00:00:34,060
(Sheldon:)that involves sleepwalking
and a 24-hour flower mart

14
00:00:34,070 --> 00:00:36,280
(Sheldon:)with a less-than-
vigilant proprietor.

15
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:38,740
(Sheldon:)Oh, Lord, my belly!

16
00:00:38,740 --> 00:00:40,590
Ever had your
appendix out?

17
00:00:40,590 --> 00:00:41,840
(Sheldon:)I haven't.

18
00:00:41,840 --> 00:00:44,290
(Sheldon:)I've been meaning to,
but who has the time?

19
00:00:44,290 --> 00:00:46,860
(Leonard:)Let's get you
to the hospital.

20
00:00:46,860 --> 00:00:51,080
(Sheldon:)So this is how it ends...

21
00:00:51,080 --> 00:00:53,220
(Sheldon:)with cruel irony.

22
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:55,500
(Sheldon:)Just as I make the commitment
to preserving my body,

23
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:59,060
(Sheldon:)I am betrayed by my appendix,
a vestigial organ.

